  "workoutProgressionHelp1": "A target is what you plan to lift. Last time is what you recorded before. Today shows only the sets you actually record. Suggestions never record a set.",
  "@workoutProgressionHelp1": {
    "description": "Progression help paragraph."
  },
  "workoutProgressionHelp2": "GoHard looks at your two most recent sessions of the same plan workout. If both have every planned set of an exercise at its target weight, with reps at the top of its range, it suggests the target plus one weight increment that you chose.",
  "@workoutProgressionHelp2": {
    "description": "Progression help paragraph."
  },
  "workoutProgressionHelp3": "It never goes further back than those two sessions, never adds sets, changes reps or swaps exercises, and never lowers a weight on its own. Timed, bodyweight and assisted exercises keep manual targets.",
  "@workoutProgressionHelp3": {
    "description": "Progression help paragraph."
  },
  "workoutProgressionHelp4": "An increment larger than 5% of the current target is not suggested automatically; you can still set the target yourself. That limit is a GoHard product choice, not a safety threshold.",
  "@workoutProgressionHelp4": {
    "description": "Progression help paragraph."
  },
  "workoutProgressionHelp5": "Reps say nothing about effort, form, pain or recovery. A suggestion is optional: review it, edit it or keep your current target. Nothing changes until you confirm.",
  "@workoutProgressionHelp5": {
    "description": "Progression help paragraph."
  },
  "workoutProgressionHelpSources": "Published guidance: the 2009 ACSM position stand describes raising the load by about 2–10% once you can do one or two reps more than your target in two consecutive sessions. The 2026 ACSM position stand advises progressive resistance training, and notes that continued overload matters mainly for longer-term progress. GoHard's rule (the top of your range in your last two sessions, one increment you chose, at most 5%) is its own product choice; neither paper tests or validates it.",
  "@workoutProgressionHelpSources": {
    "description": "Sources paragraph of the progression help. Keep the facts and years exactly."
  },
